course: dictionary
lesson: 14113
title: Meteoric: fast as a shooting star
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head. Meteoric is one of them. A meteor is a bright streak of light that flashes across the night sky very fast. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «The young singer had a meteoric rise to fame.» The words rise to fame tell you someone became famous, and the picture of a flash tells you it happened very quickly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The young singer had a very fast and sudden rise to fame.» It still makes sense, so meteoric means very fast and sudden here.
explain: The word also has a science meaning. «Meteoric dust» is dust that comes from space rocks, called meteors and meteorites. Some ancient iron tools were made from meteoric iron, which came down from space. The clues are in the words: meteor, space, and iron.
fact: Meteoric means very fast and sudden, like a flash.
fact: «A meteoric rise» means someone became famous or successful very quickly.
fact: In science, meteoric means to do with meteors, which are streaks of light made by space rocks.
fact: «Meteoric dust» and «meteoric iron» come from space rocks.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The young singer had a meteoric rise to fame.» What does meteoric mean here? | Cold and wet | Very slow and steady | *Very fast and sudden | Sleepy and quiet
exercise: «Some ancient iron tools were made from meteoric iron.» Where did this iron come from? | *Space rocks | The bottom of the sea | Mud from the garden | Melted sweets
exercise: Which sentence shows something meteoric? | *A bright light shot across the night sky in a flash | The snail crawled slowly across the lawn | The cat slept by the warm fire | The river flowed gently past the farm
test: «Her song went viral and she had a meteoric success.» What does meteoric mean? | Made of wood | Slow and steady | Lost and unknown | *Very fast and sudden
test: What is meteoric dust? | Dust from under the ocean | *Dust that comes from space rocks | Dust from inside a volcano | Dust from the kitchen floor
exam: «Sam's meteoric rise in the spelling bee surprised everyone.» What does meteoric mean in this sentence? | Gentle | Slow | *Quick and sudden | Noisy
